<title>UK: UK clears BICC consortium's naval dock buy.</title>
<headline>UK clears BICC consortium's naval dock buy.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain has approved the proposed acquisition of Devonport Royal Dockyard Plc by a consortium of U.S. offshore equipment group Halliburton, engineering firm Weir Group Plc and industrial group BICC Plc.</p>
<p>In a statement issued on Thursday the Department of Trade and Industry said it had decided not to refer the transaction to the Monopolies and Merger Commission.</p>
<p>The nuclear submarine dockyard has been managed by the same consortium for some time and has won a number of contracts for Royal Navy refitting work.</p>
<p>The OFT had initally called an inquiry into the deal to consider if it had negative implications for competition or was otherwise against the public interest.</p>
